.TH TUI_TABROW_INIT 3 2026-10-25 "libtuikit 0.8" "libtuikit Manual"
.SH NAME
tui_tabrow_init, tui_tabrow_set, tui_tabrow_set_active, tui_tabrow_active,
tui_tabrow_count, tui_tabrow_handle, tui_tabrow_render, tui_tabrow_format \-
the tab row of a screen with sub-views
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <tuikit/tabrow.h>
.PP
.BI "void tui_tabrow_init(tui_tabrow *" tr );
.BI "int  tui_tabrow_set(tui_tabrow *" tr ", const char *const *" labels ", int " n ", int " active );
.BI "void tui_tabrow_set_active(tui_tabrow *" tr ", int " i );
.BI "int  tui_tabrow_active(const tui_tabrow *" tr );
.BI "int  tui_tabrow_count(const tui_tabrow *" tr );
.BI "tui_tabrow_result tui_tabrow_handle(tui_tabrow *" tr ", const tui_event *" ev );
.BI "void tui_tabrow_render(tui_tabrow *" tr ", tui_canvas " c );
.BI "int  tui_tabrow_format(const tui_tabrow *" tr ", int " cols ", char *" out ", size_t " outsz );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tui_tabrow
draws the tabs of a screen with sub-views on one row.
Each tab is its label between two blanks, with one blank between tabs.
The active tab is drawn in the role
.B tab.active
with bold and underline added, the others in
.BR tab.inactive ,
so the active tab never depends on colour alone.
.PP
.BR tui_tabrow_init ()
makes an empty row.
.BR tui_tabrow_set ()
sets the labels (an array of at most
.B TUI_TABROW_MAX
(64) strings; neither the array nor the strings are copied) and the active
index, which is clamped to the range; it fails with
.B EINVAL
for more tabs, a NULL array or a NULL label.
Controls in a label are drawn as blanks.
.BR tui_tabrow_set_active ()
moves the active tab (clamped);
.BR tui_tabrow_active ()
and
.BR tui_tabrow_count ()
read it back.
.PP
When the tabs are wider than the canvas the row scrolls: the active tab is
always whole on the row (it is cut with an ellipsis only when it alone is
wider than the room), the first and last column are kept for the marks
\(lq\[u2039]\(rq (tabs hidden before the window) and \(lq\[u203A]\(rq (tabs
hidden after it), and a step to a neighbouring tab moves the window no further
than needed.
.PP
.BR tui_tabrow_handle ()
moves the active tab on Tab (next) and Shift-Tab (previous), both wrapping,
and on the digits 1 to 9 (that tab, when it exists), and returns
.BR TUI_TABROW_CHANGED ;
any other event, or a key that changes nothing, is
.B TUI_TABROW_IGNORED
and the program's.
.PP
.BR tui_tabrow_render ()
draws on the first row of the canvas, over its whole width.
.BR tui_tabrow_format ()
writes the same row as plain text for
.I cols
columns, without trailing blanks; it returns the length, or \-1 when
.I outsz
was too small (the text is then cut at a character).
.SH RETURN VALUES
.BR tui_tabrow_set ()
returns 0, or \-1 with
.BR errno .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libtuikit (7),
.BR tui_statusline_init (3),
.BR tui_scheme_style (3)
